<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldSteamLock.xml                 UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S1 "the boil layer — standing steam" (spec
  §S1: "the ruled RM_GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather... as a permanent
  biomeMapConditions entry... forced RUT_ScaldSteam... No damage fields — the
  steam is clean; the WATER burns.").

  conditionClass = RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather
  (ALPHA_MECHANICS_KIT_1, ruled and already shipped/built — this def only
  configures it via EnvironmentalWeatherExtension). Wired onto RUT_TheScald
  via a MayRequire-gated PatchOperationAdd
  (Patches/RUT_ScaldSteamLock_BiomeWiring.xml), not a direct XML edit to the
  BiomeDef — a plain <li>RUT_ScaldSteamLock</li> baked into
  RUT_TheScald.xml's biomeMapConditions would be a dangling cross-reference
  if mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is ever absent from the active mod
  list (same caution FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1's continuation pass already
  applied to this exact file family, for the same reason).

  🔴 "Configured clear spells" (spec's own S1 text, citing §9's "a still day
  that shows the wrecks"): GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather.ForcedWeather()
  was read in full this pass (Source/GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather.cs)
  and returns `ext.forcedWeather` UNCONDITIONALLY — there is no randomized
  or periodic lapse hook in the shipped, ALREADY-RULED class. Adding one
  would mean changing shared behaviour used by every other kit that consumes
  this same generic (miasma, forge, scarlands, sump all reference
  EnvironmentalWeatherExtension in their own kit specs) for one biome's
  flavor beat — out of this pass's scope, and not done blind. "Still day"
  ships as flavor description only this pass; a literal periodic weather
  lapse is an honest gap, not silently added to the shared class or silently
  dropped from the record.

  No damage/hediff/rot/plant-kill/density fields set (all left at their
  EnvironmentalWeatherExtension defaults, i.e. no effect) — the sheet is
  explicit the steam itself is clean; only the water burns.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldSteamLock</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather</conditionClass>
    <label>the boil's breath</label>
    <description>Standing steam over the Scald, endless and clean — it never rains here, and it never stops.</description>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <allowUnderground>true</allowUnderground>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.EnvironmentalWeatherExtension">
        <forcedWeather>RUT_ScaldSteam</forcedWeather>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
